%%abcts a per-PITCH notehead style, which is the ONE decoration inside brackets that is
%%abcts not the chord's (abc_parse_music.js:375-379). The engraver reads it per head
%%abcts (abstract-engraver.js:679), and three OTHER quantities read the head it picks:
%%abcts the up-stem's x is heads[0].w, the ledger's width is the MAX over the loop.
X:1
T:style on the lowest head
L:1/8
K:C
[!style=harmonic!CEG]2 [C!style=x!EG]2|

X:2
T:style on a head needing a ledger
L:1/8
K:C
[!style=x!C,EG]4 [C,EG]4|

X:3
T:two styles in one chord
L:1/4
K:C
[!style=x!C!style=triangle!EG]2 [CEG]2|

X:4
T:a style beside an ordinary decoration on another head
L:1/8
K:C
[!>!C!style=harmonic!EG]2 [!>!CEG]2|

X:5
T:down-stemmed, where heads[0] is not the stem's
L:1/8
K:C
[!style=harmonic!ceg]2 [ceg]2|

X:6
T:a style on a whole note and on a half
L:1/1
K:C
[!style=x!CEG] [!style=harmonic!CEG]|

X:7
T:a styled head under a tie and a slur
L:1/8
K:C
([!style=x!CEG]2-[CEG]2)|

X:8
T:a style with the element's own style beside it
L:1/8
K:C
!style=x![!style=harmonic!CEG]2 [CEG]2|
